Jahshaka patch 0055 — a Rectangle2D is born with geometry.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this. It touches a file no other patch in the stack touches
(`OgreMain/src/OgreRectangle2D2.cpp`).

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325; audit
SPECS/audits/ENGINE_WORKAROUNDS_TO_PATCHES_2026-09-15.md finding F16; the trap
is recorded in the workspace CLAUDE.md as a hard-won fact). `Rectangle2D`'s
constructor initialises `mChanged` and `mGeometryFlags` and leaves `mPosition`,
`mSize` and `mNormals` UNINITIALISED. `initialize()` fills the vertex buffer
from those members, and `setGeometry()` only raises the dirty flag — so a quad
built the obvious way (`initialize()` then `setGeometry()`) draws from whatever
the stack held, and the only thing in the engine that ever calls `update()` is
`SceneManager::_renderPhase02` on its OWN sky quad. Every other Rectangle2D in
a process therefore renders garbage geometry, silently, unless its creator
happens to know to call `update()` by hand — which is how Jahshaka's sun disc
was written, after the symptom ("a quad that never draws") cost a lane an
afternoon.

This is a trap fix, not a line-count saving: the engine keeps its explicit
`update()` (correct use of the API either way), and the next quad anybody adds
— here or upstream — starts from the full-screen geometry that is what every
user of this class has wanted so far, which is also exactly what
`SceneManager::setSky` sets. The corner rays are zeroed rather than guessed;
they are meaningful only under `GeometryFlagNormals`, and four uninitialised
rays are the same trap one level down.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and `git apply
--reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree;
`--engine-selftest` byte-identical (`b55e2d5d…`) — every quad Jahshaka creates
already sets its own geometry. The behavioural gate is `sky.*` (the sun disc
and the analytic sky are the two quads in the tree) and `test_engine`.

--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreRectangle2D2.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreRectangle2D2.cpp
@@ -44,8 +44,25 @@
         MovableObject( id, objectMemoryManager, manager, 10u ),
         Renderable(),
         mChanged( true ),
-        mGeometryFlags( 0 )
+        mGeometryFlags( 0 ),
+        // A FULL-SCREEN QUAD, because initialize() fills the vertex buffer from these
+        // two members and they used to be uninitialised: setGeometry() only raises
+        // mChanged, and the only thing in the engine that ever calls update() is
+        // SceneManager::_renderPhase02 on its OWN sky quad -- so any other Rectangle2D
+        // (a second sky, a sun disc, a debug quad) drew from whatever the stack held,
+        // silently, unless its creator knew to call update() by hand. This is the
+        // geometry SceneManager's sky sets, i.e. the one every user of this class has
+        // wanted so far.
+        mPosition( -1.0f, -1.0f ),
+        mSize( 2.0f, 2.0f )
     {
+        // The corner rays are zeroed rather than guessed: they are only meaningful
+        // under GeometryFlagNormals, whose only fillers are setNormals() and update(),
+        // and a quad that draws with four uninitialised rays draws NOTHING -- which is
+        // the same trap one level down.
+        for( size_t i = 0u; i < NumCorners; ++i )
+            mNormals[i] = Vector3::ZERO;
+
         // Always visible
         Aabb aabb( Aabb::BOX_INFINITE );
         mObjectData.mLocalAabb->setFromAabb( aabb, mObjectData.mIndex );
